      "writtenOn": "2022-12-01T18:11:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Discard shouldn\u0027t be a soft reset case.  We\u0027ll just have to try the message again later.\n\nThere\u0027s a chart in the PD spec `6.11 Message Discarding` you can read to get a sense of how the discarding works.  Since this is the first message of an AMS, it\u0027s okay if the partner interrupted to send something of its own.  We should just try starting our AMS again later.\n\nFor protocol error, usually the `pe_report_error()` function handles that for most states with exceptions for states where something special is necessary.",
      "revId": "23a2c3afc4c2eea24a12bbf6cc77f6e89e72fd88",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
